{
  "duration": 75.439,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.339,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.879,
      "end": 3.0,
      "text": "It's time to solve"
    },
    {
      "start": 3.579,
      "end": 4.339,
      "text": "one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.719,
      "end": 8.96,
      "text": "Now in this problem, we are standing at a point which is 10 root 3 meters away from a tower."
    },
    {
      "start": 9.539,
      "end": 11.659,
      "text": "The angle of elevation to the top of the tower"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.219,
      "end": 12.36,
      "text": "is"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.699,
      "end": 13.42,
      "text": "60 degrees."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.859,
      "end": 16.079,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find the height"
    },
    {
      "start": 16.44,
      "end": 17.1,
      "text": "of the tower."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.459,
      "end": 18.879,
      "text": "Let the height of the tower be"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.239,
      "end": 19.299,
      "text": "h."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.799,
      "end": 20.6,
      "text": "Also imagine a"
    },
    {
      "start": 21.079,
      "end": 22.639,
      "text": "right-angled triangle here."
    },
    {
      "start": 23.079,
      "end": 25.559,
      "text": "The height of the tower becomes the opposite side."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.959,
      "end": 28.739,
      "text": "The horizontal distance, which is 10 root 3 meters,"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.179,
      "end": 30.659,
      "text": "becomes the adjacent side."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.439,
      "end": 33.899,
      "text": "Since we know the opposite side and the adjacent side,"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.34,
      "end": 37.119,
      "text": "the trigonometric ratio we should use is 10."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.759,
      "end": 41.059,
      "text": "We know 10 theta is equal to opposite side upon adjacent side."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.559,
      "end": 41.979,
      "text": "So here,"
    },
    {
      "start": 42.52,
      "end": 49.959,
      "text": "10 60 degree is equal to h upon 10 root 3. Now, we already know one important value, 10 60 degree is equal to root 3."
    },
    {
      "start": 50.459,
      "end": 54.059,
      "text": "Putting this value into the equation, we get root 3 is equal to"
    },
    {
      "start": 54.36,
      "end": 55.899,
      "text": "h upon 10 root 3."
    },
    {
      "start": 56.259,
      "end": 58.539,
      "text": "Now multiply both sides by 10 root 3."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.879,
      "end": 64.339,
      "text": "This gives us h is equal to root 3 multiplied by 10 root 3. After simplifying this,"
    },
    {
      "start": 64.939,
      "end": 66.699,
      "text": "h is equal to 10 multiplied by 3,"
    },
    {
      "start": 67.099,
      "end": 67.359,
      "text": "which is"
    },
    {
      "start": 67.72,
      "end": 68.459,
      "text": "30 meters."
    },
    {
      "start": 69.239,
      "end": 69.619,
      "text": "Hence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 70.0,
      "end": 72.559,
      "text": "the height of the tower is 30 meter."
    },
    {
      "start": 73.199,
      "end": 75.439,
      "text": "So the correct option is option D"
    }
  ],
